<section class="shell band">
  <h1>Reem Glasco, LPC-S</h1>
  <div class="answer">
    <p>Reem Glasco is a Licensed Professional Counselor Supervisor in Texas, license 66562, and
    has held supervisor status since 2009 with over fifteen years of clinical experience. She
    is a NARM therapist, a Somatic Experiencing Practitioner (SEP), EMDR certified and an
    EMDRIA Approved Consultant. She was a Clinical Partner at Capital Area Counseling from 2021
    to 2025 and practices from Cedar Park, Texas, working online statewide.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="split">
    <div>
      <h2>How I work</h2>
      <p>My NARM approach is an invitation to be curious about your patterns, and about how
      they keep you from being present in your own life. Where did I learn this? How was it
      serving me? How does being present give me a choice about which path leads to thriving?</p>
      <p>My EMDR work is IFS-informed, which means the protective parts of you get consulted
      before anything gets processed, and my emphasis is on phases one and two where that
      agreement is built. It is weighted toward stabilization: acute stress, ongoing stress,
      overwhelm, loss. My Somatic Experiencing approach meets shock trauma in a titrated way,
      slow and gentle, building your window of tolerance rather than testing it.</p>
      <p>I teach effortless self care through walk and mindful therapy, and I run mindful trail
      retreats for interns, associates and therapists, where we explore being present and what
      gets in the way of it.</p>
      <p>I am also an LPC supervisor. Supervision is online, and I offer mindful retreats for
      associate therapists to expand their personal and professional awareness in the field.</p>
      <p>You can also find me on
      <a href="https://www.psychologytoday.com/us/therapists?search=reem+glasco">Psychology Today</a>.</p>
    </div>
